[gd_scene load_steps=15 format=3]

; PAINTED STORYBOOK -- VERTICAL SLICE
;
; A separate scene. scenes/main.tscn, the village, CVC Land and every original
; asset are untouched and still run; nothing here is wired into the game.
;
; Everything on screen is new except the camera and the control scheme, both of
; which are the SHIPPING ones on purpose: environment/fixed_camera.gd at its
; production pitch 30 / yaw 30 / zoom 9, and ui/touch_controls.tscn, so the
; assets are judged at the size and angle a child actually sees, and so touch,
; keyboard and gamepad can all be tried on the new Chuck.
;
; LIGHTING. Lower than scenes/main.tscn's, with filmic tonemapping added. The
; storybook assets arrive with their own ambient occlusion and value variation
; already baked into the albedo, so lighting them as hard as the old untextured
; primitives needed blew every light surface out -- the meadow went fluorescent
; and the cottage plaster went white.
;
; Composition is laid out in SCREEN axes and converted to world coordinates --
; at yaw 30 one unit of world +X is not one unit of screen right, and placing
; scenery by world coordinates at this angle gives a scene that is accidental
; rather than composed. See art_src/README.md.

